.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt DTFL_COLLECTION_INDEX_NEW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_collection_index_new ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_index_free ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_index_extend_using ,
.Nm dtfl_prefix_extender_free ,
.Nm dtfl_collection_extend
.Nd worst-case-optimal multi-way joins by prefix extension
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/dogs.h
.Ft dtfl_collection_index *
.Fn dtfl_collection_index_new "dtfl_collection *c" "const dtfl_type *kt" "const dtfl_type *vt"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_collection_index_free "dtfl_collection_index *idx"
.Ft dtfl_prefix_extender *
.Fn dtfl_collection_index_extend_using "const dtfl_collection_index *idx" "const dtfl_type *prefix_type" "dtfl_key_selector_fn key" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_prefix_extender_free "dtfl_prefix_extender *pe"
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_collection_extend "dtfl_collection *prefixes" "dtfl_prefix_extender *const *extenders" "size_t n" "const dtfl_type *out_type"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A delta query maintains a multi-way equijoin incrementally by keeping, for
each relation, an index of its tuples, and for each change to a relation
extending the changed prefix with the matching tuples of the other
relations.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_index_new
indexes a collection of
.Va kt Ns Li ||vt
.Pq key then value
records into the three traces an extender needs: a count trace (how many
distinct extensions a relation offers a prefix), a propose trace (the
extensions themselves) and a validate trace (whether a proposed extension
exists).
The diff class of
.Va c
must be the signed default.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_index_extend_using
builds an extender from an index and a key selector that reads the join key
out of a prefix of type
.Va prefix_type .
The key selector is what makes one index serve several positions in a
query, such as forward and reverse edges.
The extender holds its own references to the index's traces, so the index
may be freed once its extenders are built.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_collection_extend
runs the generic join.
With a single extender it is a plain propose.
With several, each prefix is annotated with every extender's offered count,
routed to the extender that offers the fewest extensions (the
worst-case-optimal choice), proposed from that one, then validated against
every other extender; the per-extender results are concatenated.
The output records are
.Va prefix Ns Li || Ns extension
of
.Va out_type .
The caller still owns
.Va prefixes
and the extenders.
.Pp
A key selector
.Pq Vt dtfl_key_selector_fn
reads the join key out of a prefix record and writes its bytes to
.Va key ,
storing the length through
.Va klen ;
.Va key
has room for at least
.Va cap
bytes.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_collection_index_new
and
.Fn dtfl_collection_index_extend_using
return handles the caller frees with
.Fn dtfl_collection_index_free
and
.Fn dtfl_prefix_extender_free .
.Fn dtfl_collection_extend
returns a new
.Vt dtfl_collection
the caller frees with
.Fn dtfl_collection_free .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_delay_neu 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_dogs_propose 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_time_altneu 3
.Sh STANDARDS
A C11 port of the dogsdogsdogs
.Pa src/lib.rs .
